-- title:
--   Crossing points are rational over the inertia ring O
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N_0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, i.e. such that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; assume the residue field $\kappa_A$ of $A$ has characteristic $q$ and is algebraically closed, and that the residue map $A \to \kappa_A$ is surjective. Let $\mathfrak P$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN` for the Igusa-type model $X(N_0q) \to \operatorname{Spec}(R_q)$. Write $F$ for the fixed field of `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms obtained as the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ inside its decomposition subgroup, and let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with a ring isomorphism $e_O$ onto the valuation ring $A \cap F$ (the comap of $A$ along $F \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$), whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$. Let $\rho_O : R_q \to O$ be a ring homomorphism which, composed with $e_O$ and the inclusions $A\cap F \subseteq F \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, recovers the structure map $R_q \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ send $o$ to the residue class in $\kappa_A$ of the image of $e_O(o)$ in $A$. Finally let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔓.comp (ResidueField ↥A) (toκ.comp ρO) 0` and `𝔓.comp (ResidueField ↥A) (toκ.comp ρO) 1` attached by the package to the base change of the model along $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$, and let $x$ be the image of $n$ under the first projection followed by `𝔓.comp … 0` followed by the base-change morphism `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`, a point of $\mathfrak X_O$, the pullback of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_O)$. The assertion is that the composite $$O \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} O,\mathcal O) \longrightarrow \Gamma(\mathfrak X_O,\mathcal O) \longrightarrow \mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_O,x} \longrightarrow \kappa(x),$$ formed from the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, the top-degree section map of the second projection, the germ at $x$ on the whole space and the residue map of the local ring, is surjective.
--
--   This is the rationality statement for the crossing (non-smooth) points of the fibre: the residue field at such a point is generated by the image of the inertia ring $O$, so the crossing is $\kappa$-rational over the base. It is used in the analysis of the node coordinates and the chart presentation of the special fibre ([`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_chartPresentation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_chartPresentation)), where an étale-local description $xy = t$ of the crossings at such points is obtained.
